-- title:
--   Finite chart is dense in a fibre without isolated points
-- statement:
--   Let $R$ be a commutative ring, $F$ a field equipped with an $R$-algebra structure and $j \in F$ a nonzero element. Write $A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ for `chartAlgFin R F j`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j$, and $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ for `chartAlgInf R F j`, the subalgebra of elements of $F$ integral over the $R$-subalgebra generated by $j^{-1}$; it is assumed that $A_{\mathrm{inf}}$ is an $R$-algebra of finite type. Let $\kappa$ be a field with an $R$-algebra structure, and let $P$ denote the fibre product of `toBase R F j`, the structural morphism from the two-chart integral model $\mathfrak X = \operatorname{pushout}(f_{\mathrm{fin}}, f_{\mathrm{inf}})$ to $\operatorname{Spec} R$, with $\operatorname{Spec}\kappa \to \operatorname{Spec} R$. Let $c \colon \operatorname{Spec}(\kappa \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{fin}}) \to P$ be a morphism whose first projection to $\mathfrak X$ is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the inclusion $A_{\mathrm{fin}} \to \kappa \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ followed by the chart morphism `ιFin R F j` from $\operatorname{Spec} A_{\mathrm{fin}}$ into $\mathfrak X$, and whose second projection is $\operatorname{Spec}$ of the structure map $\kappa \to \kappa \otimes_R A_{\mathrm{fin}}$. Assume no singleton $\{x\}$, for $x$ a point of $P$, is open. Then the image of $c$ on underlying topological spaces is dense in $P$.
--
--   This is the level-free form of the assertion that the $j$-finite chart is dense in a fibre of a two-chart integral model: the complement of the finite chart is the locus $j = \infty$, which is finite under the stated finite-type hypothesis, so it can contain no point once the fibre has no isolated points. It is used in the construction of generic charts on the Deligne–Rapoport model at $p$ in [`ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.exists_xHDRModelAtP_atkinLehner_generic_chart).
